one of the critical goals of the project is to show that a clean-room
image generation and model generation pipeline could create the base
models from the game, or rather, something that is similar enough to
be clearly related.

the idea is to show that the path must go both ways - if we ran the
system in reverse, and heuristically guided it toward "more similar"
then could we take a game with similar mechanics, point our backwards
pipeline at it, and generate all of the models in the game from a
clean-room text description?

I don't know if this will help or hurt our legal case, but it's true,
so we should due diligence create this pipeline and follow it through.
